From f3e18f68bc2d6ff621acbbd0f7570417a9e6f718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: geoca <geoca@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:42:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Input: mshw0485_touch - prune legacy lab parameters and
 dead parity paths

Now that clean Col02 initialization, HidSpiCx SET_POWER power
management, and the in-kernel multi-touch DSP pipeline are all enabled
by default and silicon-verified, remove the obsolete Phase 70-90
diagnostic module parameters and dead code paths:

- Drop all 18 obsolete laboratory module parameters (leaving only the
  single read-only pm_sleep_mode parameter, defaulting to "off").
- Remove dead Windows multi-owner parity/CFU attach paths, legacy
  Phase 72/75 initialization branches, software-recovery toggles, and
  the unused g6ts_lifecycle_profile.h header.
- Unconditionally enable the validated header-to-body SPI cadence,
  single-response-per-IRQ pacing, READY quiesce, host-fault recovery,
  and production-v1 DSP/tracking behavior.

This cuts over 1,100 lines of obsolete code and makes the driver
self-contained with zero kernel command-line arguments required.
